Mods: {
	V2: {
		Keybinds: {
			Swallow.DisplayName: Swallow
			Regurgitate.DisplayName: Regurgitate
			Feed.DisplayName: Feed
			EatItems.DisplayName: Eat Items
			StruggleUp.DisplayName: Struggle Upwards
			StruggleLeft.DisplayName: Struggle Leftwards
			StruggleRight.DisplayName: Struggle Rightwards
			StruggleDown.DisplayName: Struggle Downwards
			StruggleSpecial.DisplayName: Special Struggle
		}

		Configs: {
			V2ServerConfig.DisplayName: Server-Side Options

			Server: {
				Insight: {
					Header:
						'''
						Insight Options
						[c/7F7F7F:(these let you make bug reports and other such things easier)]
						'''

					DebugChatMessages: {
						Label: Send Debug Chat Messages
						Tooltip:
							'''
							Displays debug messages in chat relating to the various vore mechanics.
							Note that these may spam your chat, and should only be turned on if something is wrong.
							Can help greatly in bug reporting.
							Defaults to false.
							'''
					}
				}

				Personalization: {
					Header:
						'''
						Personalization Options
						[c/7F7F7F:(these let you fine-tune the experience to your preferences without breakin' the balance of the game)]
						'''

					NoRandomGulpsAgainstPlayers: {
						Label: Selectively Hungry Town NPCs
						Tooltip:
							'''
							Prevents town NPCs from randomly eating players.
							Included for players who prefer being pred.
							Does not prevent non-town NPCs from eating players where applicable.
							Does not prevent town NPCs from randomly eating other town NPCs.
							Defaults to false.
							'''
					}

					GenderBlacklist: {
						Label: Pred Non-Preference
						Tooltip:
							'''
							Allows you to prevent preds of a certain gender from actively eating others in-game.
							Generally applies to all entities, players included. However:
							- Will not affect any in-universe establishments about predators of the blacklisted gender.
							- Does not work for hermaphrodites, androgynous menaces, or otherwise functionally-genderless individuals.
							- Certain powerful entities reserve the right and ability to completely bypass any blacklist set by this option.
							By default, does not blacklist any gender.
							'''
					}
				}

				JustForFun: {
					Header:
						'''
						Options Just For Fun
						[c/7F7F7F:(these let you tell my balance intentions to go fuck themselves and just have some dumb fun with the game)]
						'''

					DefenseInDigestionCalcs: {
						Label: Include Defense In Digestion Damage Calcs
						Tooltip:
							'''
							BALANCE BREAKAGE: High
							Determines whether or not digestion damage is affected by defense.
							Affects ALL preds, not just players.
							Defaults to true.
							'''
					}

					EasilyEdibleEmpress: {
						Label: Invoke The Second Law
						Tooltip:
							'''
							BALANCE BREAKAGE: Who cares?
							Makes it possible for the Empress of Light to fit in stomachs of any capacity, with preds of any swallow strength, and greatly increases digestion damage against her.
							Defaults to false.
							'Fairies are food, not friends or foes'
							'''
					}
				}
			}
		}

		GameTips: {
			MagicMirror:
				'''
				If you come across a Magic Mirror, using it will teleport you back to your spawn point...

				...usually. Just don't try to use it in tight, dark spaces.
				'''
			LavaAndObsidianSkinPotion:
				'''
				Obsidian Skin Potions are critically useful in exploring lava-heavy terrain, allowing the consumer to bathe in it without harm.
				They also have the side effect of allowing the consumer to drink lava freely --- though, be warned, lava is VERY fattening.
				'''
			WiresFromMechanic:
				'''
				You can buy Wires from the Mechanic and use them to create traps, pumping systems, systematic waifu-feeding factories,
				or any number of other elaborate devices designed to make eating and getting eaten even easier than it already is.
				'''
			PartyGirlNeedsLotsOfSnacksToMoveIn:
				'''
				The Party Girl won't move in unless your little stretch of the world is full of other townsfolk.
				After all, what's a party without lots of totally willing guests to...invite to it?
				'''
			PredStats:
				'''
				As a pred, you have four stats: swallow strength (GLP), acid strength (ACI), stomach strength (TUM), and absorption strength (ABS).
				Be sure to investigate what each one does, and play to your best strengths as you get ready to gulp down the universe!
				'''
			SwallowHotkey:
				'''
				By pressing the Swallow hotkey while near something, or someONE, you'd like to eat, you can send 'em right down your throat!
				Just be warned that some food won't stay down as easy as others...
				'''
			HaveARefreshingDrink:
				'''
				Bothered by the immense amounts of liquids everywhere? No worries!
				If you hold the Swallow keybind while submerged, you'll let whatever refreshing drink you're in slide right into your throat!
				Be aware, though, that some drinks are a lot more dangerous to your system...you'll need special tools to make them stomach-safe.
				'''
			RegurgitateHotkey:
				'''
				If you find that a particularly feisty meal's giving you trouble, you can always use the Regurgitate hotkey to bring them back up!

				...just be sure they don't eat you themselves after doing so. An eye for an eye'll get the whole planet mulched.
				'''
			FeedHotkey:
				'''
				If you're a preything that sees a nice tum to sleep in, feel free to use the Feed hotkey to cram yourself down its owner's throat.
				Just don't expect to NOT get churned into more fat for their frame. The majority of preds don't really care about what you want.
				'''
			ItemNomsHotkey:
				'''
				Feeling a bit hungry, but don't want to feast on the squirmy snacks all around you? Just look through your inventory!
				By holding the Eat Items keybind and pressing Swallow while hovering over an item, you can send it right into your belly!
				Several items will also have unique effects when eaten and digested...be sure to check out what your snacks do in their tooltips!
				'''
		}

		PredStatsMenu: {
			StatDescription: {
				HoldSHIFTToSeeDescription: "[c/7F7F7F:Hold LEFT SHIFT to see more detailed descriptions of the following statistics.]"

				GLP: {
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Swallow Strength (GLP)] decides how good your throat is at getting your
						meals down and keeping them there while your stomach does its thing.

						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the maximum size of prey you can swallow.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseSwallowSize} base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{SwallowSizePerLevel} per stat point invested.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the rate at which you drink liquids you are submerged in.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseDrinkRate} tiles/second base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{DrinkRatePer5Levels} tiles/second per 5 stat points invested.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the struggle "grace period" after swallowing live prey.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseStruggleGraceTime}sec base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{StruggleGraceTimePer5Levels}sec per 5 stat points invested.]
						'''

					RelevantStats: {
						Normal:
							'''
							Total GLP: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{GLPTotal}]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {GLPSpent} from permanent bonuses]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {GLPBase} from permanent bonuses]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {GLPExtra} from temporary bonuses (potions, charms, etc.)]

							{$Mods.V2.PredStatsMenu.StatDescription.HoldSHIFTToSeeDescription}
							Swallow Size: {PreySwallowSize}
							Drinking Rate: {LiquidSwallowRate} tiles/second
							Struggle Grace Period: {StruggleGracePeriod}
							'''
						Chronological:
							'''
							Total GLP: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							[c/7F7F7F:| ∞ from digesting at least one Timekeeper]

							Swallow Size: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							Drinking Rate: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Countless universes/second, should you will it]
							Struggle Grace Period: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Unnecessary]
							'''
					}
				}

				TUM: {
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Stomach Strength (TUM)] decides how good that hungry tummy of yours is at
						making sure all those tasty treats you pack into it can be successfully
						detained to be digested.

						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the maximum size your stomach can comfortably reach.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseStomachCapacity} base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{StomachCapacityPerLevel} per stat point invested.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the capacity of the stomachache meter.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseStomachacheMeterCapacity} base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{StomachacheMeterCapacityPer5Levels} per 5 stat points invested.]

						If this stat is LOWER than your prey's total STR stat, [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:struggle charts]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:between you and your belly's contents are re-weighted against you]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:proportional to the difference.]
						If this stat is HIGHER than your prey's total STR stat, [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:struggle charts]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:between you and your belly's contents are re-weighted in your favor]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:proportional to the difference.]
						'''

					RelevantStats: {
						Normal:
							'''
							Total TUM: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{TUMTotal}]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {TUMSpent} from invested stat points]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {TUMBase} from permanent bonuses]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {TUMExtra} from temporary bonuses (potions, charms, etc.)]

							{$Mods.V2.PredStatsMenu.StatDescription.HoldSHIFTToSeeDescription}
							Stomach Capacity: {StomachCapacity}
							Stomachache Meter Capacity: {StomachacheMeterCapacity}
							General Struggle Chart Difficulty: {StruggleChartEstimatedDifficulty}
							'''
						Chronological:
							'''
							Total TUM: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							[c/7F7F7F:| ∞ from digesting at least one Timekeeper]

							Stomach Capacity: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							Stomachache Meter Capacity: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							General Struggle Chart Difficulty: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Even entire universes can't "struggle" inside someone as gluttonous as you]
							'''
					}
				}

				ACI: {
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Acid Strength (ACI)] decides how good your stomach acids are at eating away
						at your prey until they just can't take it anymore, ready to be churned into a
						nutritious sludge in your gut.

						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences your base digestion tick damage.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseDigestionDamage} base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{DigestionDamagePerLevel} per stat point invested.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the rate at which your belly deals digestion damage.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseDigestionRate} ticks/second base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{DigestionRatePer5Levels} ticks/second per 5 stat points invested.]

						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Certain items, such as gold, tungsten, certain clothing pieces, and plastics,]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:cannot be properly digested by normal stomach acids alone.] In order to digest
						these items, you will need to either use external digestive aids, or upgrade
						your stomach acids in a more specialized manner.
						'''

					RelevantStats: {
						Normal:
							'''
							Total ACI: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{ACITotal}]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ACISpent} from invested stat points]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ACIBase} from permanent bonuses]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ACIExtra} from temporary bonuses (potions, charms, etc.)]

							{$Mods.V2.PredStatsMenu.StatDescription.HoldSHIFTToSeeDescription}
							Digestion Tick Base Damage: {DigestionDamage}
							Digestion Tick Rate: {DigestionRate} ticks/second
							{AcidTierWithDescription}
							'''
						Chronological:
							'''
							Total ACI: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							[c/7F7F7F:| ∞ from digesting at least one Timekeeper]

							Digestion Damage: ∞
							Digestion Damage Tick Rate: ∞
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/FFFF00:Chronological (∞)]
							Your will to gobble up the entire world, the whole of the Divine Realm included, has gone
							through in full, granting you a now-former Timekeeper's control over the very flow of time.
							What was once a living, breathing universe with countless creatures residing in it has been
							reduced to naught but pudge for your tummy, yet you're still starving.

							Thankfully, there exist a virtually infinite number of other universes out there, all with
							one newfound shared purpose: as an endless food supply for you. Your acids are reality's
							new singular constant, dissolving entire planes of existence in moments, should you will it.

							Reality is your buffet. All that exists, has ever existed, and ever will have existed is
							doomed to end up as fat for your frame in time.
							Bon appetit.
							'''
					}

					AcidTiers: {
						NormalBeta:
							'''
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/9F9F9F:Normal (1)]
							Your stomach acids are just as mundane as the next predator's. [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Bones,]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:clothing, and various other materials are easily able to survive your hungry]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:tummy, despite its best efforts to melt them down.]

							[c/601818:The next acid upgrade method has not yet been implemented!]
							[c/C03030:Please wait until a future update implements the next acid upgrade method.]
							'''
						Normal:
							'''
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/9F9F9F:Normal (1)]
							Your stomach acids are just as mundane as the next predator's. [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Bones,]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:clothing, and various other materials are easily able to survive your hungry]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:tummy, despite its best efforts to melt them down.]

							An old enchantress from Avarsici is rumored to live below the surface of the tundra.
							She's no less wise or witty for it, and may be able to help remedy this fault, for a price...
							'''
						Recursive:
							'''
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/FF4FFF:Recursive (2)]
							Your stomach acids have been enchanted to digest prey recursively as a token of gratitude from a
							rather...eccentric micro-grade fairy enchantress who now lives in the depths of the frozen tundra.
							Bones and clothing can no longer escape their fate of being fat on your frame anywhere near as easily.
							However, [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:plastics and various metals still manage to evade your gut's gastric assault with ease.]

							That said, there were advertisements in the enchantress' room about a product made and sold
							entirely within Avarsician borders which can resolve this problem...
							'''
						Royal:
							'''
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/167200:Royal (3)]
							Your stomach acids, thanks to a bioalteration spell produced and sold en masse in Avarsici's own
							borders, are now mixed with nitric acid to create what most simply call "royal acids".
							Now, nothing of this plane can escape the will of your stomach.
							However, be aware that [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:various items of otherworldly origin] are still impervious to your gastrointestinal gauntlet.
							Additionally, you still [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:cannot hold and digest the souls of your prey] without the help of a charm or pred ability.

							There is little short of a deity's blessing that could grant you greater digestive potential.
							'''
						Divine:
							'''
							Stomach Acid Tier: [c/167200:Divine (4)]
							By the will of Melodia, as gratitude for bringing her star songbird back to her, your royal acids
							have been further granted the privilege which only a Sinhunter can otherwise enjoy.
							Nothing shall escape your stomach --- you can even hold and digest non-divine souls innately, and
							not even the delicacies of the Divine Realm can outlast your supreme digestive system.
							Thus, all your battles with breakfast (and other meals) are now a war of attrition --- one which,
							should you will it, you are destined to win.

							An even greater boost would be necessary to begin digesting the souls of the Divine Realm's
							inhabitants on your quest to truly become the apex...but where would one even BEGIN to gain such
							raw, unadultered gastric strength?
							'''
					}
				}

				ABS: {
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Absorption Strength (ABS)] decides how good your digestive tract is at
						ensuring that every last (digestible) trace of your prey is properly refined into
						rich, soft cellulite to be packed onto your bottomless belly's surface (and, of
						course, any other areas of preference).

						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the speed at which your body absorbs prey.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| {BaseAbsorbRate} weight/minute at base.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{AbsorbRatePerLevel} weight/minute per stat point invested.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Influences the duration of status effects from eaten food and drink.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| +{BuffExtendPer5Levels} buff duration per 5 stat points invested.]
						[c/7F7F7F:| -{DebuffLossPer5Levels} debuff duration per 5 stat points invested.]
						'''

					RelevantStats: {
						Normal:
							'''
							Total ABS: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{ABSTotal}]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ABSSpent} from invested stat points]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ABSBase} from permanent bonuses]
							[c/7F7F7F:| {ABSExtra} from temporary bonuses (potions, charms, etc.)]

							{$Mods.V2.PredStatsMenu.StatDescription.HoldSHIFTToSeeDescription}
							Absorption: {AbsorptionRate} weight/minute
							Buffs from eaten prey have their duration increased by {BuffExtensionTime}
							Debuffs from eaten prey have their duration decreased by {DebuffDisextensionTime}
							'''
						Chronological:
							'''
							Total ABS: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:∞]
							[c/7F7F7F:| ∞ from digesting at least one Timekeeper]

							Absorption: ∞ weight/minute
							Buffs from eaten prey are infinite and infinitely stackable
							Debuffs are never gained from eaten prey at all
							'''
					}
				}
			}
		}

		PredPlayerGoals: {
			Starter: {
				Name: Starter
				Subtitle: New Pred
				Description:
					'''
					Just getting started on the wonderful world of...well, eating the
					world, one meal at a time? Here are some of the first things you
					ought to do to make sure you and your gut can be as ready as can
					be to get some proper good eats in you!
					'''

				FirstLivePrey: {
					Name: First Chyme
					Description:
						'''
						Eat and digest your first live prey.
						'We all start somewhere.'
						'''
				}

				FirstItemEaten: {
					Name: Taking Inventory
					Description:
						'''
						Pluck something out of your normal inventory and into your internal “inventory”.
						'Just couldn't wait until you found a squirmy snack to swallow, eh?'
						'''
				}

				FirstDrink: {
					Name: Taking Inventory
					Description:
						'''
						Pluck something out of your normal inventory and into your internal “inventory”.
						'Just couldn't wait until you found a squirmy snack to swallow, eh?'
						'''
				}
			}
		}

		ItemName: {
			Voraria: {
				Charms: {
					BetterDigestion: Lesser Acidic Charm
					LessStomachWeight: Lesser Disencumberance Charm
					RegenFromAbsorption: Revitalization Charm
				}
			}
		}

		ItemTooltip: {
			Generic: {
				CommonColorCodes: {
					Heal: FF3F4F
					ManaHeal: 31D1E2
					PositiveEffect: 5FFF5F
					NegativeEffect: FFBF5F
					PositiveVoreEffect: 00BF00
					NegativeVoreEffect: BF5F00
				}

				HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore:
					'''
					[c/7F7F7F:Hold LEFT SHIFT for more information on this item's exact function]
					[c/7F7F7F:Hold LEFT SHIFT and LEFT CONTROL for some neat flavor text about this item]
					'''
				EdibleFromNormalUse: Using this item causes you to eat it, but it can't be used as a mouse item

				AcidResistTier: {
					1: Immune to normal stomach acids
					2: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids
					3: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids, as well as aqua regia
				}
			}

			Vanilla: {
				Accessories: {
					Utility.ShimmerCloak:
						'''
						Grants immunity to Intangibility
						Hold <down> to temporarily bypass this immunity
						Allows you to safely drink shimmer
						'''

					Informational: {
						REK3K: Displays number of enemies, kill and meal counts, and rare creatures
						TallyCounter:
							'''
							Displays how many enemies have been killed in the world
							Displays how many entities you've digested
							'''
					}
				}

				Consumables: {
					LifeCrystal: {
						Short:
							'''
							Provides a few revitalizing effects when eaten
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {LifeCrystalEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeCrystalEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When eaten by a player, upon running out of durability:
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:increases maximum health by 20].
							- For every 3 crystals eaten total, permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increase the TUM stat by 1].
							  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {LifeCrystalsMax} crystals eaten.
							Life Crystals eaten by this character (max. {LifeCrystalsMax}): [c/{LifeCrystalsUsedColor}:{LifeCrystalsUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A mysterious crystal which forms in the deeper caverns of Terraria, drawing all
							manner of curious and craving adventurers in to examine it. Upon exposing the
							crystal to a sufficient onslaught of gastric acid, the crystal lends its power to
							the consumer, greatly increasing their vitality. The means by which this strange
							phenomenon occurs are poorly understood, but have led many to believe a powerful
							being created these crystals with the intention of leeting them be eaten by
							worldly creatures in need of strength to hunt. While this was initially thought
							to be an unfounded claim, the fact that powerful predators have caught truly
							unnaturally perfect prey in the past suggests otherwise...
							Those who have eaten Life Crystals before note that doing so feels a lot like
							eating rock candy, with a notable cherry-like flavor. The first person to do it
							ended up famous worldwide for quite some time because of it, alongside a number
							of other hilariously inept, yet somehow successful achievements. A pity he ended
							up getting gulped down and gurgled by a gleeful, gluttonous ghost.
							'''
					}

					LifeFruit: {
						Short:
							'''
							Provides a swathe of truly revitalizing effects when eaten
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {LifeFruitEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeFruitEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When eaten by a player who has eaten at least 15 Life Crystals, upon running out of durability:
							- Permanently [c/{LifeFruitHealthBonusColor}:increases maximum health by 5].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases stomach strength (TUM) by {LifeFruitStomachStrengthBonus}].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases acid strength (ACI) by {LifeFruitAcidStrengthBonus}].
							  - The above three bonuses can stack up to {LifeFruitMax} times.
							Life Fruit eaten by this character (max. {LifeFruitMax}): [c/{LifeFruitUsedColor}:{LifeFruitUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A mysterious crop only ever found in the depths of a specific jungle on Terraria,
							this delectable fruit seems like only a rare delicacy at first...but when
							sufficient residual mana sourced from Life Crystals' magic swirls within the body
							of the consumer, it bestows upon them and their stomach greater power than a Life
							Crystal ever could. Many have speculated these were coerced into growing in much
							the same way that Life Crystals are thought to have been...and given that angels
							from a plane beyond have documentedly visited our planet and even been eaten by
							particularly ambitious predators on it, this isn't such an outlandish claim.
							While rather few have managed to taste the fruit in full, due to a certain trio
							of floral females deep in the jungle craving them and those who would seek out
							their craved snacks at all times, those who have managed to gulp down these
							fruits have reported a pleasant and tasteful combination of orange and mango
							flavors as the main appeal of the Life Fruit as an exotic snack option.
							'''
					}

					ManaCrystal: {
						Short:
							'''
							Provides a handful of magically beneficial effects when eaten
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:Restores 100 mana] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Mana Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{ManaCrystalEatManaRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When eaten by a player, upon running out of durability:
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:increases maximum mana by 20].
							- For every 3 crystals total eaten, permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases the ABS stat by 1].
							  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {ManaCrystalsMax} crystals eaten.
							Mana Crystals eaten by this character (max. {ManaCrystalsMax}): [c/{ManaCrystalsUsedColor}:{ManaCrystalsUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Very commonly made and just as commonly munched on, these oversized star-shaped
							batches of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy are infused with residual mana from
							pieces of the stars above, making them readily provide those who eat them with
							additional space in their mana reserves. Many have speculated that there could be
							less eating-oriented approaches to using these, but why would you care about that
							when you can munch on such a big batch of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy?
							'''
					}
				}

				Weapons: {
					Melee: {
						CactusSword: {
							Short:
								'''
								Hurts your throat a noteworthy bit to swallow
								While digesting, enemies that hit you take damage themselves
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								When eaten:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Deals {CactusSwordSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {CactusSwordSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Thorns buff] while digesting, and for [c/FFFF7F:{CactusSwordThornsTime} seconds] longer once fully digested.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A dubiously-wieldy sword fashioned from cactus cuttings. While its prickly nature
								makes it fairly usable as a weapon, one has to wonder how it would taste...and if
								there's any way to get around the discomforting amount of spines it still has.
								'''
						}

						FruitcakeChakram: {
							Short:
								'''
								Throw it to get it as far away from yourself as possible; alternatively, you can eat it
								No matter how angry eating it makes you, it is unfortunately the best way to rid the world of this menace
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								When eaten:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Deals {FruitcakeChakramSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed, because it just tastes that bad.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {FruitcakeChakramSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed; see above
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts the Poison debuff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramPoisonTime} seconds] longer once fully digested; see above.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Wrath buff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramWrathTime} seconds] longer once fully digested, because needing to eat this thing makes one VERY angry.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A single look at this abominable crime against catering makes you wonder if it was ever supposed
								to be food in the first place. The mere THOUGHT of gracing this...THING with death by digestion
								almost seems too good a mercy for it.

								You're not alone in that assessment, either. Fruitcake was first made long ago by a rather...
								...eccentric baker in a territory previously owned by one of the many, MANY royals that have
								made their mark on Terraria over the years.

								It is now banned within any and all Avarsician borders; the very kingdom whose then-prince
								Markus Caldera originally annexed the country (and its queen) as a way to prove his worth (and,
								to his credit, he WAS successful on both fronts) as heir to the throne.
								The Apex Convocation unanimously agreed to ban it from Desperais, and despite the hundreds of
								years and countless shifts in the seat fillings that have passed since that initial ruling, that
								ban has never been lifted.
								Countless other territories outside of these two notable powers also ban it, and only ever for
								one reason: the mere existence of this concept is slander against the good name of bakers the
								planet over.

								The only use this has is as a weapon, and POTENTIALLY as emergency rations if all else is gone.
								'''
						}
					}
				}
			}

			Voraria: {
				Charms: {
					BetterDigestion: {
						Short:
							'''
							Makes your acids a little bit stronger
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your acid strength stat (ACI) by {AcidStrengthBonus}]."
						Flavor:
							'''
							A beginner-level charm designed to make the bearer's stomach acids substantially
							more potent than if they were to go without it. Very useful for first-time
							predators who could really use that extra kick to their digestive juices to
							secure their first few big meals, though sadly not particularly worthwhile past
							those starting stages.
							'''
					}

					LessStomachWeight: {
						Short:
							'''
							Makes your stomach lighter, but only if you're not too full
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight by {WeightReduction}.]
							If your stomach is at {FullnessEffectivenessLossThreshold} fullness or more, [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:this effect becomes less effective the less capacity you have to spare.]
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A beginner-level charm designed to make one's stomach less of a burden to lug
							around while it's full of sweet, sloshy calories. While it works in most cases,
							it does this by passively generating a layer of helium inside of the bearer's
							stomach; thus, if there isn't sufficient room to provide said helium deposits,
							the charm becomes substantially less effective.
							'''
					}

					RegenFromAbsorption: {
						Short:
							'''
							Grants health and mana regeneration while digesting dead prey
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:While digesting dead prey:]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Health is regenerated] at a rate of {HealthRegenerationRatio} of your [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:absorption rate].
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:Mana is regenerated] at a rate of {ManaRegenerationRatio} of your [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:absorption rate].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Effectiveness decreases if there are prey in your stomach still alive.]

							Current Regeneration ({RegenEffectiveness} effectiveness with {LivePreyRemaining} out of {PreyRemaining} prey still alive):
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:{CurrentHealthRegen} HP/sec]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:{CurrentManaRegen} mana/sec]
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							An intermediate-level charm designed to ease the long-standing issue of one's
							digestive system granting surprisingly little reprieve from the heat of battle.
							As long as a surplus of food resides in the bearer's stomach, this charm will
							convert some of the excess calories into mana to fuel a spell which revitalizes
							the bearer both physically and magically. Of course, this spell can only work
							as quickly as the bearer's belly can digest its meals.
							'''
					}
				}

				Consumables: {
					DigestionRepairScroll: {
						Short:
							'''
							Using this item requires a  will instantly relieve you of most of the downsides of predator or preything lifestyles
							When this is used, a full day must pass before another one can be used
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can only be used once at least one full day has passed since the last time it was used.
							Upon usage, it will instantly:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Fully repair all items in your inventory] that have taken digestion damage and can be repaired.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Remove all Softened stacks still applied to you] from any lingering acid burns from recent encounters.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Clear all indigestion-related debuffs you may have] from particularly troublesome meals.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							It's a scroll, inscribed with countless runes that you've never seen before;
							notably, they look surprisingly similar, yet so very different, from musical
							notes...which would help, if the scroll bothered to say anything about the actual
							composition of the piece. Whoever wrote this sheet music didn't think it through
							very well from the perspective of one who might want to play it.

							In any event, incomprehensible as it may be at a cursory glance, as you go to
							look at it closer, the runes fade into the background somewhat, and a second
							layer of text fades in which is actually comprehensible to the average person:

							[c/FF3FBF:CHORUS (sing this part, in D# major):
							From heavens inward and a cauldron outward, the Conductress' graces shall smile.
							By Melodia's song, this verse, when not wrong, shall save from a fate all too vile.

							If you near face the Veil, the edge of our great hail, when a chance predator leaves you weak,
							By Melodia's song, sing these verses along, and your strength shall return to thy peak.]

							[c/7F1F5F:POST-CHORUS (composer's note):
							But the song must rest, asleep in its nest, 'fore its strength can remend its own peak,
							So by my sacred song, don't you dare sing this wrong; I've no care for the melodically weak.]

							...you can't help but wonder if Promethia stole this from someone.
							'''
					}

					DigestionUpgradeTablets: {
						Short:
							'''
							Can only be eaten once you've fully gained the stomach-strengthening effects of Life Fruit and enchanted your stomach acids beforehand
							Permanently modifies your digestive system using a delayed-effect bioalteration spell once fully digested
							This mixes nitric acid into the structure of your stomach acid, turning it into aqua regia (royal water)
							This change makes your stomach significantly better at digesting things, and allows you to digest more things you wouldn't normally be able to
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can only be eaten once you have eaten and digested at least {LifeCrystalsMax} Life Crystals, at least {ManaCrystalsMax} Mana Crystals, and at least {LifeFruitMax} Life Fruits.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your acid strength stat (ACI) by 40.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your absorption strength stat (ABS) by 20.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Causes your stomach to bypass almost all material-based acid resistances.]
							This upgrade is permanent, but only takes effect once the pack is fully digested.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Despite how often these things were flaunted around as the future of predatory
							prowess and a marvel of modern magical bioengineering back in the day, the real
							marvel is that these somehow pose no significant health risks despite mixing an
							entire secondary acid into an already-powerful stomach. The label on the side
							suggests eating the entire pack...including the pack itself. The pack supposedly
							has much better nutritional value than the pills, so...bottoms up.
							Obtaining more than one pack of these tablets is prohibited by Avarsician law and
							punishable by...well, predominantly fucking about and learning what for. It's not
							exactly hard to guess why a spell that assumes you haven't taken the pills at all
							is bad if you've already melted down a full pack of them before.
							'''
					}
				}
			}
		}

		InfoDisplayName.TallyCounterVore: Meal Count
		InfoDisplayText.TallyCounterVore.InvalidMeal: Meal count unavailable

		StatusEffects: {
			Debuffs: {
				MoltenStomach: {
					Name: Molten Stomach
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Your stomach is getting melted from the inside by the lava you drank.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Maybe don't drink lava without a way to prevent this outcome.]
						'do you are have stupid'
						'''
				}

				ShimmeringStomach: {
					Name: Shimmering Stomach
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Your stomach is about to end up quantum-superimposed on itself.]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Don't drink shimmer without a way to prevent this outcome.]
						'Fool ya once, shame on me. Fool ya twice...'
						'''
				}

				Softened: {
					Name: Softened

					Description: {
						Base:
							'''
							A stack of this debuff is applied for every [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:{SoftenedMaxHealthThreshold} of your BASE maximum health you take in digestion damage.]
							Up to [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:{SoftenedMaxStacks}] can be applied on you (current: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:{SoftenedStacks}]).
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Decreases defense by {SoftenedDefReduction}] per stack (current: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:{SoftenedCurrentDefReduction}]).
							[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Increases taken digestion damage by {SoftenedDigestiveAid}] per stack (current: [c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:{SoftenedCurrentDigestiveAid}]).
							'''

						Flavor: {
							0: You've stayed acid-free for a good while, haven't you?
							1: You feel a light itch in a few places
							2: You're starting to itch a good deal more
							3: Your skin is starting to sting, badly
							4: Your skin feels like it's burning
							5: You feel patches of skin starting to decay
							6: Your skin is starting to melt off
							7: Your predator's stomach has picked up the pace now
							8: The muscles beneath your bones are melting away now
							9: You can barely fight the acidic onslaught anymore
							10: Say your goodbyes; they're more likely to escape this gut than you are
						}
					}
				}

				SoreThroat: {
					Name: Sore Throat
					Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Prevents swallowing anything orally]
						Does not stop other methods of consumption
						'Something's bothering your throat pretty bad'
						'''
				}
			}
		}

		Death: {
			DrownedPlayer: {
				GutSlut: {
					1: "{Player} mistook water for the stomach acid pools they're familiar with."
					2: Maybe stick to drowning in people instead of ponds, {Player}.
					3: "{Player} probably has a thing for mermaids. Unfortunately, they couldn't find any hungry mermaids fast enough."
				}
			}

			DigestedPlayer: {
				YouWereEaten: You were eaten...
				Paradox: Awfully full of yourself today, aren't you, {Player}?

				Universal: {
					1: "{Player} was eaten by {Pred}."
					2: "{Player} couldn't escape {Pred}'s stomach."
					3: "{Pred}'s stomach was the last thing {Player} ever saw."
					4: "{Player} learned the hard way that napping in a gut isn't safe."
					5: "{Pred} mulched {Player} without a second thought."
					6: "{Player} slipped down {Pred}'s throat, never to be seen again."
					7: "{Pred} had {Player} as a quick snack."
					8: "{Pred} made a meal of {Player}."
					9: "{Player} became an idiot sandwich."
					10: "{Pred} now has Exquisitely Stuffed for a while, thanks to {Player}."
					11: "{Player} became a second breakfast for {Pred}."
					12: "{Player} tried to become a gastroenterologist from memory."
					13: "{Player} mistook pearly whites for pearly gates."
					14: "{Player} is a terrible dieting advisor."
					15: "{Player} thought the Iron Maiden sounded hot."
					16: "{Player} got fucking churned lmaooo"
					17: "{Player} was mulched by {Pred}."
					18: "{Player} got got by {Pred}."
					19: "{Player} was eaten from the bottom up...or was it from the top down?"
					20: "{Player} underwent a merciful euthanasia by digestion."

					StomachSuffocation: {
						1: "{Player} ran out of air in {Pred}'s stomach."
						2: "{Pred}'s stomach didn't have enough air for {Player}."
					}
				}

				SpecificDigestionType: {
					Acidic: {
						1: "{Player}'s fruitless thrashing was finally stopped by {Pred}'s stomach acids."
						2: "{Pred}'s stomach acids were too much for {Player}."
						3: "{Player} went on the other kind of acid trip."
						4: "{Player} succumbed to {Pred}'s acids."
						5: "{Player} tried to swim in acid."
						6: "{Player}'s flesh was melted from the bone inside {Pred}'s stomach."
						7: "{Player} was transmuted into chyme by {Pred}."
						8: "{Pred}'s stomach melted {Player} down."
						9: "{Player} was dissolved by {Pred}."
						10: "{Player} got a little too soft."
					}

					Thermal: {
						1: "{Player} got torched."
						2: "{Player} was smelted by {Pred}."
						3: "{Player} burned to a fine crisp inside {Pred}."
						4: "{Player} misjudged the digestive strength of fire."
						5: "{Player} was burned to death in {Pred}'s stomach."
					}
				}

				HumanoidPred: {
					1: "{Player} became ass fat for {Pred}."
					2: "{Player} helped to widen up {Pred}'s thighs."
					3: "{Player} gave {Pred} an extra waistband size."
					4: "{Player} decided to bulk up {Pred}'s booty a little."
				}

				SpecificNPC: {
					Meteorite: {
						MeteorMarble: {
							1: "{Player} thought a Meteor Marble was crafted well enough to feed themselves to."
							2: "{Player} found a Meteor Marble that was just a little too big to handle."
							Hardcore:
								'''
								Somehow, {Player} thought it was a good idea to make a Meteor Marble big enough to fit inside.
								Fitting, then, that the last moments of their only life were spent crammed into that very same Meteor Marble.
								Nobody will ever find what remains of them...for nothing does.
								'''
						}

						MeteorMaiden: {
							1: "{Player} was helplessly smitten for a refueling Meteor Maiden."
							2: "{Player} helped to re-energize a Meteor Maiden after a long day's work by the latter."
							3: "{Player} thought a Meteor Maiden's combustion chamber looked inviting."
							4: If Meteor Maidens had a rear or thighs to add prey to, {Player} would definitely be working to fatten them up right now.
							5: A Meteor Maiden saw {Player} as a sufficient fuel source, and secured them for herself.
							Hardcore:
								'''
								A pleasant sound, almost like a belch, but bassier and rockier, rings out over the mountaintops.
								{Player} has ended up as little more than a meal for a Meteor Maiden, never to be seen again.
								Perhaps that Meteor Maiden will go on to eat a moon or seven, and countless celestial bodies beyond? Only time will tell...
								'''
						}
					}

					Townsfolk: {
						Nurse: {
							1: "{Player} made a very healthy meal for {Pred}."
							2: "{Player} helped to keep {Pred}'s belly happy and healthy."
							3: "{Pred}'s digestive system was given a check-up by {Player}."
							4:
								'''
								{Pred} lost her medical license after adding {Player} to her hips...
								...oh, wait. That's what she's qualified to do. Never mind.
								'''
							5: "{Player} is now a victim of medical mealpractice."
							6: "{Player} was quarantined."
							7: "{Pred} prescribed {Player} a one-way trip to her backside...whether they got there is another story."
							8: "{Pred} gave {Player} a thorough examination by digestion."

							NoFundsForHeal: {
								1: "{Player} couldn't pay their medical fees."
								2: "{Player} thought free healthcare exists."
								3: "{Player} tried to undercut {Pred}, and learned the hard way how bad of an idea that is."
								4: "{Player}'s insurance didn't cover digestion."
							}

							Hardcore:
								'''
								{Player} has become the newest victim of {Pred}'s medical mealpractice.
								Mind you, most healthcare packages cover digestion reformation...but {Player} forgot to buy one.
								'''
						}

						ArmsDealer: {
							1: "{Player} was locked and loaded into {Pred}'s gut."
							2: "{Pred} gave his stomach some target practice with {Player}."
							Hardcore:
								'''
								{Player} was chambered into {Pred}'s ruthless gut, never to be seen again.
								The skilled gunman simply spent the rest of his day unwinding with some relaxing target practice as his prey melted away.
								'''
						}

						Angel: {
							1: "{Player} was given a one-way ticket to the second Heaven that is {Pred}'s belly."
							2: "{Player} atoned for their sins (or, perhaps, committed more of them) within {Pred}'s confines."
							3: "{Player} will be thoroughly studying {Pred}'s internals."
							4: "{Player} was somehow a submissive enough snack to get {Pred} to melt them into gut fat. An impressive, if strange, performance."
							Hardcore:
								'''
								{Pred}'s stomach sent {Player} to Heaven...which, in her case, happens to still be her stomach.
								Ah, well. At least the rest of their days will be well-enjoyed as fat on her frame.
								'''
						}

						Stylist: {
							1: "{Player} melted inside {Pred}'s stylish stomach."
							2: '''{Pred}'s belly gave {Player} a "free" haircut.'''
							3: "{Pred} let {Player} marinate for a while in her stomach acids."
							4: "{Player} was snackrificed to {Pred}."
							5: "{Player} will look super stylish as a new layer of fat for {Pred}."
							6: "{Pred} just couldn't resist {Player}'s delectable hair."
